    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3429\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the\nauthorization of the county of Rensselaer to impose an additional one\npercent of sales and compensating use taxes\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis legislation authorizes the imposition of an additional one\npercent sales tax in Rensselaer County until November 30, 2011.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThe bill amends clause 3 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph\nof section 1210 of the tax law to authorize the continuation of an\nadditional one percent sales tax in Rensselaer County until November\n30, 2011.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation is being introduced at the request of the Rensselaer\nCounty Legislature. Under current law, Rensselaer County is authorized\nto collect an additional one percent sales tax.  This is due to expire\non November 30, 2009. This legislation is necessary to allow\nRensselaer County to continue its collection of the additional sales\ntax.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
